  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved partnerships, workers and vulnerable groups are effectively protected   from unacceptable forms of work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This CPO has 2 major objectives: 1. OSH &amp; HIV TOT implementation and 2. Disability Project: FJI/25/50/UND 
1. Strengthening OSH capacity in Fiji builds on earlier ILO supported initiatives that have positioned the country as a potential Centre of Excellence for Occupational Safety and Health in the Pacific in OSH frameworks. Building on 2025, the ILO delivered a dedicated HIV Training of Trainers programme, equipping national partners to integrate HIV awareness and prevention into workplace safety systems. Continued ILO assistance will help consolidate these gains by enhancing systems, TOT skills and enforcement mechanisms, while supporting future. 
2. Disability FJI/25/50/UND: This programme aims to enhance the rights and opportunities of persons with disabilities in Fiji, who often experience poverty, unemployment, and stigma. It focuses on accountability, equality, CRPD-compliant budgeting, and inclusive service delivery, while integrating disability considerations into national humanitarian efforts, benefiting persons with disabilities and their communities.</narrative>
  </description>
